   "id": "nazir.34b.3",
   "daf": "34b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ שְׁלֹשָׁה מִינִין אֲסוּרִין בַּנָּזִיר: הַטּוּמְאָה כּוּ׳. הַיּוֹצֵא מִן הַגֶּפֶן — אִין. גֶּפֶן עַצְמוֹ — לָא. מַתְנִיתִין דְּלָא כְּרַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר. דְּתַנְיָא, רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אוֹמֵר: אֲפִילּוּ עָלִין וְלוּלָבִין בַּמַּשְׁמָע.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The mishna taught that «three types» of actions «are prohibited for a nazirite:» Contracting «ritual impurity,» shaving, and consuming products of the vine. The Gemara infers: «That which emerges from the vine, yes,» it is included in the prohibition; however, any part of «the vine itself,» other than its fruit, «no,» this is not forbidden. The Gemara comments: «The mishna is not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Elazar.» This is «as it is taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Elazar says: Even» the «leaves and tendrils» of the vine «are included» in the prohibitions of naziriteship."
  }
 ],
